        958
      ],
      "title": "Read at most 64KiB plus one byte before parsing resume options",
      "mechanism": "The new relay calls the unchanged metadata-then-tokio::fs::read helper. A file growing or replaced after the metadata observation is read/allocated in full before the second size check. Accepted input remains capped, but the claimed bounded input read is not enforced during IO.",
      "impact": "A concurrent large-file growth/replacement can cause unbounded IO/allocation before the local API request, despite the advertised64KiB options boundary.",
      "minimal_correction": "Use a dedicated bounded read of an opened options file via AsyncReadExt::take(65537), then refuse a resulting length above65536 before constructing/sending the HTTP request. Preserve the shared strict DTO and all existing Parent helpers/API/Core bodies.",
      "needed_regression": "A meaningful options oversize refusal before connection, plus a controlled bounded-reader/growing-source seam if the IO-bound guarantee is asserted. No runtime result is claimed."
    }
  ],
